# systemd user units, whole tree. systemd is a Linux init system and no other OS has a user
# manager to read these, so on macOS and Windows the directory is 20-odd files that look
# authoritative and are never loaded. Gated as a directory rather than unit by unit: a new
# timer should not have to be remembered here to stay off the machines that cannot run it.
